          "title": "You'll want to know: palleō, pallēre",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "palleō, pallēre — \"to be pale\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ancilla timōre pallet. The maid is pale with fear."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "palleō, pallēre, palluī. English pallor comes from its noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "palleō is inherited from a Proto-Indo-European root meaning \"grey, pale\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short). English pallor comes from the noun built on it."
            }
          ]
        },
